==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Evil Aku Researcher''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat Researcher''' when obtained from [[Fury of Hell (Merciless)]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Aku Researcher's main use is to destroy [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies' [[Shield]]s, some of which can be incredibly durable otherwise despite protecting a somewhat fragile enemy. Unlike most other [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]], he doesn't require [[Cat Capsule#Rare Cat Capsules|Rare Capsules]], [[Behemoth Stone]]s or [[Talents]]. Against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]], his damage, Single Attack and [[Critical Hit|Crit]] chance make him inefficient compared to other specialized [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]]. This means that Aku Researcher's usage is mostly limited to occasionally piercing Shields, where damage matters none compared to chance and attack rate. You will also have to protect and time him well since he dies quite easily, even with his many knockbacks. Due to his Single Attack, he will also need to be supported by other attackers to clear peons from his path and give him a clear shot at Aku Shields. With proper support, he can even be a serviceable counter to [[Fallen Bear]], able to outrange him consistently and eventually destroy his Shield.

His high knockback count effectively also prevents him from being Warped, which comes in handy in [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] + Aku stages such as [[Great Barrier-free]].

==='''True Form'''===
Aside from moving much faster, which allows him to serve as a rusher in timed levels, Cat Researcher's improvements are an increase in health and more frequent attacks. The former can be decently useful, exceeding 10k at level 30. While this isn't particularly high, it could potentially allow Cat Researcher to survive an attack that would have otherwise finished him, letting him reposition with his naturally high knockback count.

The latter is considerably more useful for increased chances to land Critical Hits and pierce Shields. More specifically, he attacks every 14f instead of every 35f, or 2.5 times as fast as before. His Critter niche is accentuated and surprisingly valuable, as most other conventional critters don't have such a fast attack rate and range, making him very useful for picking off weaker Metal enemies like [[Metal Doge]] and even [[Metal One Horn]] at weaker magnifications if Cat Reseacher is boosted enough. The same can also be said for Shield Piercing, which he now does even better since usually openings don't persist, and having more chances to destroy shields makes these threats much more manageable.

Finally, Cat Researcher gains an efficient Worker Start Level Up [[Cat Combo|Combo]] with [[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Ragelan Pasalan]]. Considering how Aku stages do tend to be cash-tight at times and both units are specialized in countering enemy Shields, they can give you a great head start against tight start-offs. Although the two are much less useful in general, they are still worth bringing as these Combos can stack with the likes of [[Don't Mess With Me! (Combo)|Don't Mess With Me!]] and [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Riches]] for greater effect.

