==Trivia==
*The red text on Evil Aku Researcher's sign is upside-down katakana that translates to "''[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Devil]] Information''," while the black text translates to "''Cat Queen opens the gates to the [[The Aku Realms|Devil World]].''" Cat Queen is the Japanese name of [[Princess Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Cat]], whose description reads "''With her vast intellect (and forbidden spellbooks), she has guided the Cat Kingdom to a golden age.''"
**The red text on Cat Researcher's sign translates to "''Cat Information''", while the black text translates to "''Cats are lifeforms whose thoughts are shrouded in mystery.''"
*Evil Aku Researcher's Japanese description directly mentioned The Aku Realms before they were added to the game.
*While the word ''Aku'' (悪) is used to represent demonic enemies, it is also a Japanese word meaning "evil" or "wickedness", so Evil Aku Researcher's name could also be interpreted as "Evil Evil Researcher", rather than "Evil Demon Researcher".
*The Vortex mentioned in Aku Researcher's description may be [[Aku Cyclone]], whose own description reads "''Souls it draws inside are sent to the Aku realms to join that land's wicked armies.''"
*Aku Researcher's sign says that "Akus" ignore [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] attacks, but descriptions such as [[Aku Doge]]'s and [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]]'s have consistently used "Aku" as the plural of Aku.
*Unlike [[Ms. Sign]] and [[Angel Fanboy]], Aku Researcher has the text on his sign translated between English and other languages that can be chosen, such as Spanish and French. This does not, however, apply to Evil Aku Researcher and Cat Researcher, whose signs are in Japanese regardless of version or language.
**As a result, Aku Researcher is the only unit whose appearance changes at all between these languages.
*Aku Researcher is listed as a source for the information in [[Wicked Face]]'s description.
*Aku Researcher does a complete 180 as he evolves. He starts as an ally of the [[Cat Units|Cats]] who is researching the Aku, but eventually becomes corrupted during his research and serves the Aku by researching Cats instead.
**His loyalty to the Aku may still be brought into question, however, as despite his transformation, he continues to aid the Cat Army's efforts against Aku enemies through his impressive Shield Piercing capabilities. This could imply a mere fascination to his research rather than complete servitude.
*Unlike [[Angel Fanboy]], his advice is actually true under all circumstances; there is currently no Aku/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy in the game.

